+# Verified Global / partner scope candidate
+
+Paired producer: dc51d8920dd25d4c11bf48737cdca31ada3e8a63. Portal baseline fac3b6a0c7cb55dd75d3c190a1382ce710030381.
+
+Real authenticated page defaults eligible internal actors to Global; partner actors to their verified firm. Global is an explicit directory context, never a synthetic report grant. Select Firm is populated from server outcomes; each search page and accepted selection uses its own explicit registry tenant and opaque firm/revision binding. Client/account narrowing uses existing Resolution. Identity/session changes replace the page query cache and selection state. Partial and unavailable firm outcomes remain visible.
+
+`server-wire.json` is synthetic output of the actual candidate directory Entry. `context.test.ts` runs it through the real LiveClient and envelope parser. `mounted.mjs` mounts the real page under controlled AuthContext and transport; it is not a live authentication or production proof.
+
+Validation: typecheck, targeted ESLint, production build PASS. Focused client plus field-map tests: 13 PASS; mounted page PASS; existing header-race and browse-race controls PASS. Build emits existing CSS URL / chunk-size warnings. Broad legacy fe-s-13 run is not claimed green: isolated producer fixture paths and old operation/census expectations need separate paired-layout classification.
+
+No deployment or vendor calls. The downstream generation custody owner/profile extension is a separate admitted candidate and is not proved by this directory/browser test.
